[latex]\begin{aligned}
&\text{External work done} \\ &=\text{load} \times \text{deflection} \\ &=W_{u}\times \Delta =W_{u}\times \frac{L}{2}\times \theta\\ &=\frac{W_{u}L\theta }{2}
\end{aligned}[/latex] [latex]\begin{aligned}
&\text{Internal work done}\\ & =\text{moment} \times \text{rotation} \\ &=M_{P}\theta +M_{P}\left ( \theta +\theta \right )\\ &=3M_{P}\theta
\end{aligned}[/latex] By principle of virtual work, External work done = Internal work done [latex]\; \frac{W_{u}L\theta }{2}=3M_{P}\theta[/latex] [latex]\; W_{u}= \frac{6M_{P}}{L}[/latex]

